Alternately, when you attempt to wield something of which there are
multiples, it just splits one off at that point and gives it a separate
inventory letter.  Then corrosion behaves as you would expect -- the one
in your hand is corroded as-wielded, and the rest as-appropriate.

The player would have to drop/repickup, or bag/unbag the one to restack
them, but in general if you're taking a single dagger out of a stack to
wield, I don't think this is such a big hardship.

